<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91693" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῠρί-καυστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>burnt in fire</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.564
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.922a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Vett.Val.
				127.32
			</span></i>; in late 
				Ep.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῠρί-καυτος</span></b> , Epic. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Arch.Pap.</u>
				7.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				10.74
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>caused by a burn</i> (or <i>scald</i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.384
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φλυκταινίδες ὥσπερ π</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				2.1.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. [ἕλκη</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.68.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				866a6
			</span></i>; later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρίκαυτα ἕλκεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SA</u>
					1.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρίκαυστον, τό</span>, <i>plaster for a burn</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.19.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ign.</u>
				38
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ π. ἔμπλαστρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Asclep.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.525
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>inflammatory</i>, in the form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-καυτος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				85c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Asin.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>inflamed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερῴα πυρίκαυτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
					<u>Or.</u>
					49(25).30
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
